-- models/engine/profile.rofl — HYPOTHESES ABOUT A RUN, AS RULES THE RUN'S PROFILE JUDGES (docs/cli.md, *The
-- profile of an evaluation*). Load it beside any world: its rules read the book `profile`, so the engine writes it
-- after the first run, and these rules run over it in the round after. Everything here is in the book `profile`, and
-- what the pack says leaves its own rules out.
--
-- Two kinds of rule. A VERDICT reads the meters and names a rule or a premise the author should look at:
--   scan        a premise that read far more rows than it let through, and why (a relation too small for an index,
--               or a selective premise with nothing bound)
--   rescan      a premise read whole on every firing of a rule that fires more than once (read = fires x rows)
--   rederives   a rule most of whose conclusions were already known (conc > 2 x fresh)
--   barren      a rule that read and concluded nothing
--   hot         a rule that read a quarter or more of all the rows read
-- A FORECAST says, from the shape of a rule and the sizes of what it reads, how many rows its head can hold; the
-- profile's `rows` judges it: `forecast_off` where the head holds more than the forecast (the hypothesis is false),
-- `forecast_loose` where it holds less than a quarter (the bound is too weak to plan by). The forecasts, each an
-- upper bound:
--   projection  one arm, one positive premise, no negation: rows of that premise
--   join        one arm, two positive premises sharing a variable: |A| x |B| / max(distinct values at the shared slot)
--   product     the same with no shared variable: |A| x |B|
--   closure     the transitive closure of Base (one base arm, one recursive arm): distinct(Base, 1) x distinct(Base, 2)
--   chain       the closure of a Base whose both columns are keys: n(n+1)/2 paths at most
-- And a GROWTH class, which only two runs of different sizes can judge (rust/rofl/tests/profile_model.rs):
--   per_row     a recursive rule solved news first: what it reads grows with its head
--   per_round   a recursive rule kept in written order: what it reads grows with its head times its rounds
--   kernel      a closure the kernel answers: the rule fires never, the kernel's cost is not in the profile
--
-- The kernel's own program (safety.rofl) comes profiled too, `program[profile](R, safety)`, with its rules reflected
-- by the profile itself (`kernel_premise`, `kernel_head`), so the same verdicts fall on it; its forecasts need
-- `concludes` and `rows` of the kernel's book, which the profile does not carry, and are not made.
--
-- The reflection is read slot by slot, as examples/shapes/shapes.rofl reads it: `premise_lit(R, K, $lit(Rel, Book,
-- Args, Tense))`, K from 1, the arguments a `$cons` list. A hypothesis that needs what is not here (which variables
-- a premise binds at run time) is not written: a forecast that cannot be judged is not a forecast.

-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ the reflection, by slot
pf_lit[profile](R, K, Rel, B, As) :- premise_lit(R, K, L), L = $lit(Rel, B, As, _).
-- the kernel's own program, safety.rofl, reflected by the profile since no world of a user's reflects it
pf_lit[profile](R, K, Rel, B, As) :- kernel_premise[profile](R, K, L), L = $lit(Rel, B, As, _).
pf_tail[profile](R, K, 1, As)     :- pf_lit[profile](R, K, _, _, As).
pf_tail[profile](R, K, J, T)      :- pf_tail[profile](R, K, I, $cons(_, T)), J is I + 1.
pf_slot[profile](R, K, J, A)      :- pf_tail[profile](R, K, J, $cons(A, _)).
pf_var[profile](R, K, J, V)       :- pf_slot[profile](R, K, J, $var(V)), not pf_meta[profile](V).
pf_var[profile](R, K, J, V)       :- pf_slot[profile](R, K, J, A), A = $var(W), W = $var(V).
pf_meta[profile](V)               :- pf_slot[profile](_, _, _, $var(V)), V = $var(_).
pf_head[profile](R, Rel, B)       :- conclusion_lit(R, 1, L), L = $lit(Rel, B, _, _).
pf_head[profile](R, Rel, B)       :- kernel_head[profile](R, L), L = $lit(Rel, B, _, _).
pf_npos[profile](R, N)            :- pf_lit[profile](R, _, _, _, _), N is count(K : pf_lit[profile](R, K, _, _, _)).
pf_neg[profile](R)                :- premise_lit(R, _, L), L = $not(_).
pf_neg[profile](R)                :- kernel_premise[profile](R, _, L), L = $not(_).
pf_arms[profile](Rel, N)          :- concludes(_, Rel), N is count(R : concludes(R, Rel)).
recursive[profile](R)    :- pf_head[profile](R, Rel, B), pf_lit[profile](R, _, Rel, B, _).
-- the pack's own rules conclude in this book; they are profiled too, and left out of what it says
pf_own[profile](R)       :- pf_head[profile](R, _, profile).
-- the facts a relation was given, beside what its rules conclude: the census counts them (`base`), since a count over
-- asserted_by per fact read 51 million rows at 250 files of vscode (rows x group)
pf_base[profile](Rel, B, N) :- base[profile](Rel, B, N), N > 0.

-- ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ verdicts
scan[profile](R, K, Rel, Read, Out) :- read[profile](R, K, Read), yield[profile](R, K, Out), pf_lit[profile](R, K, Rel, _, _),
                                       Out > 0, Read > Out * 3, Read >= 16, not pf_own[profile](R).
scan_why[profile](R, K, small_relation) :- scan[profile](R, K, Rel, _, _), pf_lit[profile](R, K, Rel, B, _), rows[profile](Rel, B, N), N < 16.
scan_why[profile](R, K, selective)      :- scan[profile](R, K, Rel, _, _), pf_lit[profile](R, K, Rel, B, _), rows[profile](Rel, B, N), N >= 16.

rescan[profile](R, K, Rel) :- fires[profile](R, F), F > 1, not pf_own[profile](R), pf_lit[profile](R, K, Rel, B, _), rows[profile](Rel, B, N),
                              read[profile](R, K, Read), Read is F * N.

rederives[profile](R, Conc, Fresh) :- conc[profile](R, Conc), fresh[profile](R, Fresh), Fresh > 0, Conc > Fresh * 2, not pf_own[profile](R).

rule_read[profile](R, T)  :- fires[profile](R, _), not pf_own[profile](R), T is sum(X ; K : read[profile](R, K, X)).
read_total[profile](T)    :- T is sum(X ; R : rule_read[profile](R, X)).
barren[profile](R, Read)  :- fires[profile](R, F), F > 0, conc[profile](R, 0), rule_read[profile](R, Read), Read > 0, not pf_own[profile](R).
share[profile](R, Pct)    :- rule_read[profile](R, X), read_total[profile](T), T > 0, Pct is X * 100 / T.
hot[profile](R, Pct)      :- share[profile](R, Pct), Pct >= 25.

-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- forecasts
pf_one[profile](Rel, R)   :- pf_arms[profile](Rel, 1), concludes(R, Rel), not pf_own[profile](R).
pf_two[profile](R, A, BA, B, BB) :- pf_npos[profile](R, 2), pf_lit[profile](R, K1, A, BA, _), pf_lit[profile](R, K2, B, BB, _), K1 < K2.
pf_shared[profile](R, D)  :- pf_npos[profile](R, 2), pf_var[profile](R, K1, J1, V), pf_var[profile](R, K2, J2, V), K1 < K2,
                    pf_lit[profile](R, K1, A, BA, _), pf_lit[profile](R, K2, B, BB, _),
                    distinct[profile](A, BA, J1, DA), distinct[profile](B, BB, J2, DB), DA >= DB, D = DA.
pf_shared[profile](R, D)  :- pf_npos[profile](R, 2), pf_var[profile](R, K1, J1, V), pf_var[profile](R, K2, J2, V), K1 < K2,
                    pf_lit[profile](R, K1, A, BA, _), pf_lit[profile](R, K2, B, BB, _),
                    distinct[profile](A, BA, J1, DA), distinct[profile](B, BB, J2, DB), DB > DA, D = DB.
-- a shared slot no row holds divides nothing: the join is then a product of an empty relation
pf_div[profile](R, D)     :- pf_shared[profile](R, _), D is max(X : pf_shared[profile](R, X)), D > 0.

pf_rules[profile](Rel, N, projection) :- pf_one[profile](Rel, R), pf_npos[profile](R, 1), not pf_neg[profile](R), pf_lit[profile](R, _, P, B, _), rows[profile](P, B, N).
pf_rules[profile](Rel, N, join)       :- pf_one[profile](Rel, R), not pf_neg[profile](R), pf_two[profile](R, A, BA, B, BB),
                                         rows[profile](A, BA, NA), rows[profile](B, BB, NB), pf_div[profile](R, D), N is NA * NB / D.
pf_rules[profile](Rel, N, product)    :- pf_one[profile](Rel, R), not pf_neg[profile](R), pf_two[profile](R, A, BA, B, BB),
                                         rows[profile](A, BA, NA), rows[profile](B, BB, NB), not pf_div[profile](R, _), N is NA * NB.

pf_tc[profile](Rel, Base, BB) :- pf_arms[profile](Rel, 2), concludes(R1, Rel), not pf_own[profile](R1), pf_npos[profile](R1, 1), pf_lit[profile](R1, _, Base, BB, _), Base != Rel,
                        concludes(R2, Rel), recursive[profile](R2), pf_npos[profile](R2, 2), pf_lit[profile](R2, _, Base, BB, _).
pf_rules[profile](Rel, N, closure) :- pf_tc[profile](Rel, Base, BB), distinct[profile](Base, BB, 1, D1), distinct[profile](Base, BB, 2, D2),
                                      N is D1 * D2, not pf_keyed[profile](Base, BB).
pf_rules[profile](Rel, N, chain)   :- pf_tc[profile](Rel, Base, BB), pf_keyed[profile](Base, BB), rows[profile](Base, BB, M), N is M * (M + 1) / 2.
pf_keyed[profile](Rel, B) :- rows[profile](Rel, B, M), distinct[profile](Rel, B, 1, M), distinct[profile](Rel, B, 2, M).

-- what the rules can add, plus what the relation was given
forecast[profile](Rel, N, Kind) :- pf_rules[profile](Rel, M, Kind), pf_head[profile](R, Rel, B), pf_base[profile](Rel, B, K), N is M + K.
forecast[profile](Rel, N, Kind) :- pf_rules[profile](Rel, N, Kind), pf_head[profile](R, Rel, B), not pf_base[profile](Rel, B, _).

forecast_off[profile](Rel, Kind, N, Actual)   :- forecast[profile](Rel, N, Kind), pf_head[profile](R, Rel, B), rows[profile](Rel, B, Actual), Actual > N.
forecast_loose[profile](Rel, Kind, N, Actual) :- forecast[profile](Rel, N, Kind), pf_head[profile](R, Rel, B), rows[profile](Rel, B, Actual), Actual * 4 < N.

-- --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- growth
growth[profile](R, kernel)    :- recursive[profile](R), written_order[profile](R, closure).
growth[profile](R, per_round) :- recursive[profile](R), written_order[profile](R, Why), Why != closure.
growth[profile](R, per_row)   :- recursive[profile](R), not written_order[profile](R, _), not pf_own[profile](R).
